{
 "spec": "services",
 "file": "relay",
 "notes": "O-3 padding buckets, O-5 relay authority, O-6 relay selection, bootstrap gateway configurations and witnesses. O-6 picks come from a fixed stream, SHA-256(hum/relay-pick/1 \u2016 seed \u2016 uint32be(counter)) read as 32-bit draws with rejection sampling over the set in the order given (shipped relays, then the context's): a reference device so the vectors are deterministic, not a protocol rule; a phone uses its CSPRNG and only the set membership and the re-pick rule are normative.",
